AB  - Based on the rapid development of generative artificial intelligence (GAI), its impact on higher education has attracted widespread attention. Beyond the academic community, the public perspective on this issue have also begun to draw researchers’ interest. However, existing studies mostly focus on a single perspective, with few offering a comparative analysis that integrates both. Thus, this study draws on 169 articles from the CNKI platform and 8,499 public discussion posts to analyze the concerns surrounding GAI in higher education across two perspectives, employing methods such as complex network analysis, topic modeling, and large language models. From the perspective of public discussion, large language models are further used to identify user roles, revealing differences in attitudes and focal points among various groups regarding GAI in education. On this basis, the study systematically compares the similarities and differences in concerns between academic research and public discussion, providing a reference for understanding the social impact of GAI in higher education and for informing relevant decision-making.
