AB  - This systematic literature review examines the impact of generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) on the creative thinking of learners in STEAM and interdisciplinary higher education contexts. A total of 57 studies, published between 2022 and 2025, were included based on predefined inclusion and exclusion criteria. The review reveals that GenAI generally exerts a positive effect on learners’ creative thinking, enhancing divergent and convergent thinking, interdisciplinary integration, and problem-solving abilities. Its effectiveness, however, is moderated by tool type, task complexity, and learner characteristics, highlighting the conditional and ecological nature of its impact. The review identifies key application strategies and mechanisms through which GenAI supports creativity, including cognitive scaffolding, iterative refinement, collaborative engagement, personalized support, and development of digital literacy and critical thinking. Theoretical frameworks underpinning these studies encompass constructivism, knowledge construction, self-determination theory, project-based learning, design thinking, and technology acceptance models. These findings provide a theoretical and practical foundation for leveraging GenAI to foster creativity in STEAM learning within higher education.
